# Local patches carried on top of the vendored checkout.
#
# FIVE LIVE OVERLAYS, not all in the fork yet: four behavior fixes and one
# cross-cutting incident replay suite. They are committed directly into
# `Raven-main/` (with a refreshed `subagents/TREE_HASHES`), so this file records
# every affected path plus WHAT and WHY rather than an appliable diff. A
# re-vendor must re-apply each overlay that the selected source does not yet
# contain.
#
# The first two fix defects the 2026-09-01 dispatched-run report raised (host
# TUI orchestrating a DAG, Raven-Code driven as an ACP sub-agent over OpenRouter
# claude-opus-5). Each behavior change is written to be upstreamable as-is.
#
# 1. Empty-response recovery must not prefill an Anthropic model.
#    `raven/agent/loop/recovery.py`, `raven/agent/loop/main.py`,
#    `raven/providers/{base,litellm_provider,lazy,per_model_provider}.py`,
#    `tests/test_agent_loop_empty_recovery.py`.
#    A thinking-only turn was recovered by re-feeding the model its own
#    reasoning as a trailing assistant message. Anthropic rejects that request
#    while thinking is on, and through a gateway the rejection arrived as a
#    stream that never produced a byte, so the turn hung to the wall clock.
#    Providers now declare `supports_assistant_prefill`; when it is refused the
#    recovery uses the act-now nudge, then the plain retry budget.
#    Report item 1.
#
# 2. The stream needs its own idle timeout.
#    `raven/config/schema.py`, `raven/providers/{base,litellm_provider}.py`,
#    `raven/cli/_helpers.py`, `tests/test_litellm_provider_timeout.py`.
#    `chat_stream` waited the whole request budget for every chunk, so with
#    `llmCallTimeout: 1800` a dead stream cost half an hour.
#    `streamIdleTimeout` (default 180s, 0 disables) decides whether the stream
#    is dead; the request budget is enforced separately so a backend that
#    trickles forever is still bounded. Report item 2.
#
# 3. A submitted ACP turn keeps the policy captured when it was accepted.
#    `raven/acp/methods.py`, `raven/agent/loop/main.py`,
#    `tests/test_acp_methods_session_modes.py`,
#    `tests/test_agent_loop_session_policy.py`. A concurrent
#    `session/set_mode` now affects the next turn instead of changing a queued
#    turn while it is running.
#
# 4. The ACP configuration refuses unknown keys.
#    `raven/config/schema.py`, `tests/test_config_acp_modes.py`. A misspelled
#    `defaultMode` used to be ignored and silently selected the first declared
#    mode.
#
# 5. The dispatched-run incident is replayed through the real streaming path.
#    `tests/test_agent_loop_incident_replay.py`. It covers the Anthropic
#    thinking-only recovery, the separate stream idle deadline, and the
#    deployed configuration defaults across overlays 1 and 2.
#
# Also carried: the ACP session-modes work (effort tiers) from local fork
# branch feat/acp_session_effort_modes at c0197f8e. Those four commits DO live
# in a fork branch, and that branch is based on the same 3edd204f baseline as
# this snapshot, so their content applies on its native base. A future
# re-vendor from a branch that contains them absorbs them cleanly.
#
# History: every patch this file used to carry is in the source lineage. The
# remote fork branch (github.com/TongLi31/Raven, feat/acp_worktree_integration)
# is at 9bda1403; the vendored snapshot came from its local continuation.
# The GitLab workflow does not publish that continuation to GitHub.
#
# 1. everos timestamp coercion -> fork commit 31fd7f3
#    ("fix(memory): coerce a message timestamp to the ms epoch for everos").
#
# 2. in-workspace session migration removal -> the fork dropped
#    `SessionManager._migrate_in_workspace_sessions` (and inverted the two
#    upstream tests that asserted the migration happens); the vendored tree
#    carries no migration code to remove.
#
# 3. ACP session working-directory binding (turn workdir, coding tools,
#    identity prompt, bootstrap segment, per-checkout checkpoints) -> fork
#    commit d076432 ("feat(agent): adopt the workspace-inheritance hotfix
#    semantics at the source"), which ports the gitlab hotfix
#    (fix/raven_code_workspace_init_hotfix @9cd1047d) verbatim where the fork
#    had not already implemented it.
#
# A future local fix should be committed to the fork first whenever possible;
# only a change that cannot live upstream belongs here.
